A||||4||Sillhouette.com||Story from the Detroit show (long)||||1||
Z||000000||Sillhouette.com||06-17-2000||08:55 PM||||Well I made it back from the show....<P>There I saw the turbo setups that a lot of you were talking about and it does not look good one bit.  There are too many fittings too many parts to go wrong not to mention that the owner I talked to had no clue about what he was talking.  <BR>You tell me:  I asked him how many horses does his turbo 2.8 made ..... the answer was 320Hp next question was the compression in the combustion chamber 8.2 and the pressure of the turbo   11psi.  Man that seems like a lot of HP for basically nothing.  If this car puts out 320 HP than the RSM supercharged unit at 9.5 compression and 10 psi should be able to orbit earth and we know that the RSM setup puts out 280HP. There was a nice Turbo setup it has a name forgot it .    The install was nice but still too many parts and tubes to go wrong.  You can't be worrying about these things when you're blasting around the circuit or at the 1/4 mile.  RSM supercharger all the way for me.  <P>Now on the way home the RSM boys have scored two kills.  First one was against a brand new Alero with the big deal 3.5 twin chained cam engine in it.  Sorry not good enough. I don't know much about the low end power because when we met I was at 170 KPH than I passed him at 190KPH (that is where the fiero gauge stops reading speed) and still pulled very hard til 5000 rpm and the needle floating straight down.  I think those cars are limited to 220 kph which I'm sure I passed no problem.   <BR>The second kill was against an Infinity I 45 once again no contest at 190kph the thing fell back and I know he was trying because of the whine of the engine and the black smoke that came out of the exhaust when I was behind him and he tried to pull away.  <BR>The supercharged fiero was just idling behind uss all the way.  The owner said that he never had more than 5 psi on the boost gauge.  The max is 10psi.  <BR>Sorry for the long post ....  <P>Fire away your comments question    <P>Cheers||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero mistress||06-19-2000||02:36 PM||||Good kills!  one question, how do you translate KPH to MPH?  Sounds like you were going REALLY fast!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||06-19-2000||03:17 PM||||Well let's see<P>170 kph = 110 mph<BR>190 kph = 120 mph<BR>220 kph = 140 mph<P>Hope this helps<P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000003||Earne||06-20-2000||07:09 AM||||Sillhouette, were you at the Michigan Fiero Fest at Sellers Pontiac?  I was in that show.  If same show, did you see the silver GT with more engine chrome than the front bumper of a '58 Buick?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sillhouette.com||06-20-2000||02:58 PM||||Yes I have seen it and talked to the owner as well.  The chroming is not a bad idea since keeping a polished engine compartment requires repolishing every week or so.  The only drawback is that they could not get the part of the intake that has a hole in it properly done and also his dogbone was not chromed but everything else was.  I also looked at the prices for the chromed stuff and man are they ever expensive.  And that is US dollars so canadian dollar is unexplainable.   <P>Later||||reg||1
